+	<!-- custom: Directional river-map symbols in this order: open water without a river edge, lake without a river edge, land without a river edge, river on the plot's southern boundary, river on its eastern boundary, then both boundaries. Blank ocean, visible lakes and quiet dotted land preserve landmass and inland-water outlines; river symbols take priority over that background. The default = and ! make both river orientations substantially heavier than dotted land, while | remains reserved for the picture frame. Civ4 exposes the two stored boundaries as isNOfRiver and isWOfRiver because the plot is respectively north or west of the river. This preserves which orthogonal movement/attack crosses a river at native resolution instead of merely marking riverside plots; resampled cells report whether either orientation occurs anywhere within them. (ChatGPT-5.6-Sol + GPT-5.6-Sol) -->
